  "_notes": [
    "FTC vote: chronicle shows an initial 3-3-2 jury tie (Mickey: Dave/Shawn/Topher; Sky: Blaineley/Max/Sugar; Ryan: Amy/Scarlett), broken by 3rd-place Ryan casting the deciding vote for Mickey (final 4-3). Data file expresses the same result as '4-3-2 (tiebreak)'. No contradiction; both agree Mickey wins over Sky with Ryan as kingmaker.",
    "Dave.betrayedBy includes both Sky and Mickey. Sky is the discrete chronicle event (F6/ep12: Sky played the Campers idol on Sugar and flipped to vote Dave, an Alliance #3 mate). Mickey is included per the data file's 'biggestBetrayal' award (Mickey slowly replacing the early Lulu Dave/Mickey core with the Mickey/Ryan endgame axis) — this is a slow narrative drift, not a single backstab; Mickey actually voted Sugar (not Dave) at F6.",
    "idoledOut=true assigned to Beardo (ep3), Samey (ep4), and Blaineley (ep10): each was eliminated because an idol negated the votes that would have gone to the intended target (Blaineley's own idol saved her in ep3/ep4; Mickey's idol saved Ryan in ep10), leaving the counter-target as the effective boot. Matches the data file's '★ (idol negation)' vote notations.",
    "Josee (ep6) marked blindsided (ambushed) but idoledOut=false: Rodney used Knowledge Is Power to steal her Lulu idol pre-vote, then played it on himself; Josee was the actual vote target (5 effective votes) after losing her protection, rather than being redirected around by an idol negating votes cast on her.",
    "Ella (ep2) and Jasmine (ep5) left as blindsided=false: both were cut in low-vote chaos rounds (Ella after her own failed Shot in the Dark; Jasmine in a straightforward 2-1 swing-vote), with no narrative shock/ambush framing.",
    "No showmances occur anywhere in the chronicle; all showmance arrays are empty.",
    "votesAgainstTotal values taken from the data file placement notes (authoritative season totals) since the chronicle's per-tribal tallies are partial; chalWins uses the data file's 'immunity wins' figures.",
    "Advantages that are not idol-type (Rodney's Knowledge Is Power, Max's Safety Without Power, Mickey's Goodwill, Blaineley's Inheritance, the tribe/merge Amulets, and Samey's unused swap-two advantage) are not counted in idolsFound/idolsPlayed. Exception: Shawn's Amulet reached the 1-holder stage and became a full Hidden Immunity Idol, so it is counted as an idol he found and played."
  ]
